  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "UI: Change how system default locale is set",
  "description": "In [QTBUG-82831](https://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-82831) it was mentioned that the current way of setting the system default locale in Wireshark is suboptimal:\n\n> `QLocale(QLocale::system().name())` is a compiled-in locale object, based on platform-independent CLDR data, that does all its lookups without making any system calls. `QLocale::system()` is a very different creature indeed: many of its lookups go via system native APIs that may report user-customization of settings that deviate from what is usual for the CLDR locale identified by its name(). Indeed, in some cases, the system may support a locale that CLDR does not; for example, it might support a UK-specific German-language locale, `de_GB`, potentially with custom complications configured by the user. In such a case, `QLocale(QLocale::system().name())` would be `QLocale(\"de_GB\")` which would in fact resolve (via generic \"`de`\") to effectively \"`de_DE`\", with no UK-specific details or user-configured custom settings, where `QLocale::system()` would (as far as it can) reflect the system-configured UK details along with any custom settings set by the user.\n\nSo, this changes (in case the system default language is used) the locale to be set with `QLocale::system()` and then `localeLanguage` is derived from it, instead of setting first `localeLanguage` and then setting the system locale based on that.\n\nIf you understood what is said above, please review.",
